{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And on the Sabbath day, two lambs.</b> On the three festivals, and also on the new moon, and likewise on Rosh HaShanah and Yom HaKippurim, you find each day seven lambs apart from the continual burnt offering. But here, on the Sabbath, He did not command them to offer more than two lambs, and they must be equal for the commandment, as they said in the second chapter of Sheqalim: the additional offerings certainly require equality. And the meaning of 'for the commandment' — not as a disqualification. And the reason there were only two is that the Sabbath's honor is doubled — זכור and שמור, את שבתותי תשמרו — and therefore all the matters of the Sabbath come doubled: the עומר is doubled, its warnings are doubled, its reward is doubled, its punishment is doubled, its song is doubled, its offering is doubled. <b>By way of the Midrash:</b> the Holy One, blessed be He, said: I do not want you to bring Me on the Sabbath more than yourselves — just as you have two meals, so too I have two lambs. Thus far." "<b>And two tenths.</b> Corresponding to the showbread. And he did not mention here for the Sabbath והקריתם nor והקרבתם, because they did not offer the additional offering in the wilderness, for they were not commanded until now."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:36:42.316351694Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}